WEBVTT

00:02.211 --> 00:04.589
<i>♪ it seems today
 that all you see ♪</i>

00:04.633 --> 00:07.638
<i>♪ is violence in movies
 and sex on tv ♪</i>

00:07.765 --> 00:11.355
<i>♪ but where are those
 good old-fashioned values ♪</i>

00:11.441 --> 00:14.361
<i>♪ on which we used to rely? ♪</i>

00:14.448 --> 00:17.786
<i>♪ lucky there's a family guy ♪</i>

00:17.872 --> 00:21.335
<i>♪ lucky there's a man who
 positively can do ♪</i>

00:21.421 --> 00:22.881
<i>♪ all the things that make us ♪</i>

00:22.966 --> 00:24.134
<i>♪ laugh and cry ♪</i>

00:24.261 --> 00:30.148
<i>♪ he's... A...
 Fam... Ily... Guy! ♪</i>

00:35.036 --> 00:36.746
-Hey, meg, what's up?
-[gasps]

00:36.831 --> 00:39.043
A cool kid said, "what's up?"

00:41.843 --> 00:44.179
Oh, it was just a dream.

00:46.854 --> 00:49.734
[gasps] goldy, no!

00:49.778 --> 00:53.158
Ugh. Fifth one this week.

00:54.831 --> 00:57.752
Oh, my god! Mr. Clompers.

00:57.838 --> 00:59.714
[grunts]

00:59.800 --> 01:01.594
Stay with me, mr. Clompers.

01:01.680 --> 01:02.596
[exhales]

01:02.723 --> 01:04.726
Stay with me,
you son of a bitch.

01:04.854 --> 01:05.812
[exhales]

01:05.897 --> 01:08.192
[neighs]

01:08.278 --> 01:11.158
Oh, there's only one way
to turn this day around.

01:11.285 --> 01:13.580
Crouch behind a dumpster
in the back of quiznos

01:13.665 --> 01:16.628
And wait for the half-eaten subs
to be thrown out.

01:20.639 --> 01:23.686
Yep, looks like things are
finally starting to turn around

01:23.771 --> 01:26.150
For the meg-a-rino.

01:27.237 --> 01:28.822
Hey, what are you doing?

01:28.950 --> 01:30.744
I'm not a dumpster.
Put me down.

01:30.829 --> 01:31.913
Aah!

01:31.998 --> 01:34.126
-Man, this job sucks.
-I don't know.

01:34.212 --> 01:36.173
Ladies running with trash bags
and no bras on

01:36.258 --> 01:37.342
Is pretty cool sometimes.

01:37.469 --> 01:38.553
-[running footfalls]
-[woman] wait.

01:38.680 --> 01:39.847
Right on cue.

01:39.975 --> 01:42.812
And now the mind creates
scenarios and so forth.

01:46.657 --> 01:48.618
Hey, what are you doing home
from work?

01:48.703 --> 01:51.082
Ah, some sicko called in
a bomb scare.

01:51.209 --> 01:52.627
Then they confiscated
everyone's phones

01:52.712 --> 01:54.339
And I was told to
take the day off.

01:54.424 --> 01:56.260
Peter, did you call in
the bomb scare?

01:56.387 --> 01:58.014
God, you sound just like them.

01:58.141 --> 01:59.935
For the last time, maybe.

02:00.020 --> 02:01.855
Well, since you're home,
you can watch

02:01.900 --> 02:03.986
My daytime shows with me.

02:04.113 --> 02:05.739
-[phone rings]
-hello.

02:05.826 --> 02:07.326
There's a bomb in the tv.

02:07.413 --> 02:09.123
Leave the remote
and exit the room.

02:09.292 --> 02:11.962
<i>Nice try, but we're watching
 the view.</i>

02:12.132 --> 02:13.507
<i>Welcome to the view.</i>

02:13.592 --> 02:15.929
Today we're talking
about mansplaining.

02:16.016 --> 02:17.433
Meghan mccain, you go first.

02:17.560 --> 02:19.145
I thought meghan mccain quit.

02:19.231 --> 02:21.066
Oh, yes, she did.
They replaced her

02:21.193 --> 02:24.198
With a dozen feral cats
in a quinceañera dress,

02:24.284 --> 02:25.284
And no one can tell
the difference.

02:25.411 --> 02:28.959
[cats mewling, screeching]

02:29.086 --> 02:30.922
The cats have
an important dead dad,

02:31.050 --> 02:33.218
So we got to hear 'em out.

02:33.305 --> 02:35.265
<i>[announcer]
 it's the kelly clarkson show.</i>

02:35.351 --> 02:37.019
She's got a show now?

02:37.063 --> 02:38.940
Yes, and she's actually
very funny,

02:39.026 --> 02:41.279
If you're a woman who claps
when the plane lands.

02:41.365 --> 02:44.077
Give me that thing. Aren't there
any daytime tv shows

02:44.120 --> 02:45.163
Hosted by men?

02:45.332 --> 02:46.666
Peter, are you kidding me?

02:46.752 --> 02:49.214
Conversations between men
are boring.

02:49.299 --> 02:51.218
I've heard what you
and the guys talk about.

02:51.303 --> 02:52.554
Me and the guys would be great

02:52.640 --> 02:53.766
At hosting one of these shows.

02:53.893 --> 02:55.728
We talk about interesting stuff
all the time.

02:55.814 --> 02:57.482
Just this past weekend,
we were talking about

02:57.567 --> 02:59.654
How a lot of people don't know
which one is chip

02:59.739 --> 03:00.531
And which one is dale.

03:00.658 --> 03:02.076
Well, it's actually very simple.

03:02.161 --> 03:04.999
Chip's nose is black,
and dale's nose is red.

03:05.127 --> 03:06.085
And if you need help
remembering,

03:06.170 --> 03:07.463
You say "chocolate chip."

03:07.590 --> 03:09.385
The chipmunks were easier
because they had

03:09.429 --> 03:10.512
Big letters on their shirts.

03:10.597 --> 03:12.517
-But that's Tuesday's show.
-Oh, please.

03:12.644 --> 03:14.855
All men run out of things
to say to each other

03:14.941 --> 03:16.400
-After 20 minutes.
-Oh, yeah?

03:16.486 --> 03:18.071
Well, if guys are so bad
at talking,

03:18.157 --> 03:19.867
How come regis philbin
is still yapping?

03:19.994 --> 03:22.330
[regis]
so joy hands me a box,
and I open it,

03:22.499 --> 03:25.337
And it's the same darn sweater
from last christmas!

03:25.506 --> 03:27.091
Can you believe that? Coming up,

03:27.218 --> 03:28.511
<i> Angel's david boreanaz.</i>

03:28.597 --> 03:31.602
Look at kathie lee.
She's fanning herself.

03:37.575 --> 03:38.910
Whoa, meg, what happened to you?

03:38.995 --> 03:41.248
Yo, I straight-up thought
that was post malone

03:41.375 --> 03:42.292
For a hot second.

03:42.420 --> 03:44.631
I just had the worst day
of my life.

03:44.759 --> 03:47.262
Now, if you don't mind, I'm
gonna bake cookies from scratch

03:47.348 --> 03:49.308
And eat them until I puke.

03:49.352 --> 03:50.811
Meg, I think what you're
going through are

03:50.939 --> 03:52.232
Typical teenage emotions.

03:52.400 --> 03:55.030
Trust me, everything will change
when you go to college.

03:55.157 --> 03:57.452
Speaking of,
guess who got a letter

03:57.579 --> 04:00.333
From the university
of rhode island today.

04:00.419 --> 04:01.336
Wait, what?

04:01.505 --> 04:04.217
And it came in a big envelope.

04:04.303 --> 04:06.180
You know what that means.

04:06.307 --> 04:07.976
Finally some good news.

04:08.103 --> 04:09.354
"from the office of admissions

04:09.439 --> 04:10.983
At the university
of rhode island."

04:11.110 --> 04:12.695
Wow, so official.

04:12.780 --> 04:15.868
"hey, sorry, we ran out of
small envelopes.

04:15.954 --> 04:18.082
You didn't get in."

04:18.209 --> 04:21.423
[crying]

04:21.508 --> 04:23.051
Meg, I'm so sorry.

04:23.138 --> 04:27.604
I just have to accept it,
I'll never be happy.

04:27.689 --> 04:29.817
[sobbing]

04:33.745 --> 04:36.666
A talk show for men?
That's a great idea.

04:36.752 --> 04:38.545
Yeah. Imagine getting paid
to talk about stuff

04:38.631 --> 04:40.508
We already talk about
around this table.

04:40.594 --> 04:43.306
<i>Hey, that could be the title.
 Bar table talk.</i>

04:43.391 --> 04:44.601
Oh, guys, check it out.

04:44.686 --> 04:46.814
Tom tucker's wasted
at the bar again.

04:46.900 --> 04:48.318
Put on channel six.

04:48.445 --> 04:51.992
I-I want to see what doppler
those dinks are working with.

04:52.078 --> 04:53.872
A 3000?! Ha!

04:53.999 --> 04:57.046
What, are they telling us
the weather in 2004?

04:57.215 --> 04:58.716
Hey, fellas, I'll be right back.

04:58.802 --> 05:01.347
Boy, it's fun to fantasize
about having a talk show.

05:01.432 --> 05:03.352
But, sadly, that's all
it's gonna be,

05:03.437 --> 05:05.439
'cause ain't nobody
putting four guys

05:05.567 --> 05:08.656
-With zero experience on tv.
-Yeah, you're right.

05:08.783 --> 05:10.868
Start thinking of warm
to hot topics, fellas.

05:10.995 --> 05:12.288
What are you talking about?

05:12.374 --> 05:13.750
I just spoke to tom tucker.

05:13.836 --> 05:15.797
A few months ago
I did him a big favor,

05:15.841 --> 05:18.261
And he said if there's anything
he could ever do for me,

05:18.346 --> 05:20.641
Just ask, so I just asked.

05:20.727 --> 05:21.852
And he said yes.

05:21.937 --> 05:25.318
Gentlemen, say hello
to the hosts of your new

05:25.487 --> 05:27.072
Channel five daytime talk show.

05:27.158 --> 05:28.743
Oh, my god, that's amazing.

05:28.828 --> 05:30.204
This is awesome. Wait, joe,

05:30.331 --> 05:32.251
What was the favor
you did for tom tucker?

05:32.420 --> 05:34.840
I mustache-sat for him
over the holidays.

05:35.886 --> 05:38.557
<i>We said rise of gru
and then bed.</i>

05:38.642 --> 05:40.854
That was the deal we made.

05:40.939 --> 05:42.273
[mustache squeaks petulantly]

05:42.358 --> 05:43.735
I'm sorry you're having
a hard time.

05:43.820 --> 05:46.032
I'm having a hard time, too.

05:49.459 --> 05:51.294
Hey, what the heck
are you guys doing?

05:51.379 --> 05:52.839
<i>Those are my cookies.</i>

05:52.966 --> 05:55.220
Meg, these are literally
the best cookies

05:55.305 --> 05:56.514
I've ever had in my life.

05:56.642 --> 05:58.268
Yeah, they're incredible.

05:58.395 --> 05:59.646
Did you switch up the recipe?

05:59.732 --> 06:01.275
No, I don't think so.

06:01.361 --> 06:03.071
So good, meg. I'd have another,

06:03.198 --> 06:05.701
But I got to see dean later.
Dean's my trainer.

06:05.787 --> 06:07.581
Guy kicks my freakin' ass.

06:07.708 --> 06:09.168
You must have done
something different.

06:09.295 --> 06:10.713
These are fantastic.

06:10.799 --> 06:12.801
Hmm.

06:12.928 --> 06:15.516
I think my tears
falling into the batter

06:15.601 --> 06:17.729
Must have made these cookies
taste different.

06:17.773 --> 06:20.193
Not different, delicious.

06:20.279 --> 06:23.826
Last week, dean was saying I'm
the most ripped guy he trains.

06:23.953 --> 06:25.121
Off the record, of course.

06:25.290 --> 06:27.083
Meg, I think this could be
the start of a business.

06:27.169 --> 06:29.798
People would pay a premium
for cookies this good.

06:29.925 --> 06:30.675
Really?

06:30.802 --> 06:33.014
Oh, a business is a lot of work.

06:33.099 --> 06:36.689
Unless maybe...
You guys want to help out?

06:36.858 --> 06:38.735
-I'd be happy to.
-I'll do it.

06:38.905 --> 06:41.115
So Monday, Wednesday and fridays
are dean days.

06:41.242 --> 06:44.164
Other than that, I'm down.
I'm in ketosis, by the way.

06:44.291 --> 06:45.751
This is exciting, you guys.

06:45.878 --> 06:47.421
We just have to find a way
to get the word out

06:47.506 --> 06:48.633
About these cookies.

06:48.718 --> 06:50.595
I don't think we'll have
to worry about that.

06:50.681 --> 06:52.808
I just got an email back
from the one show

06:52.852 --> 06:56.149
That'll put our product in front
of the entire country.

06:56.235 --> 06:58.404
<i> Long hallway shark tank.</i>

06:58.532 --> 06:59.741
♪ ♪

06:59.826 --> 07:01.746
<i>[announcer]
first up, meg griffin and family</i>

07:01.873 --> 07:05.630
<i> With a new twist
 on a popular snack.</i>

07:09.808 --> 07:11.810
♪ ♪

07:27.305 --> 07:29.267
♪ ♪

07:35.783 --> 07:37.577
Hello, sharks. I'm here to--

07:45.681 --> 07:47.641
We have so many
new cookie orders.

07:47.769 --> 07:49.605
Which means we've got
a lot of baking to do.

07:49.690 --> 07:50.607
Let's get going.

07:50.692 --> 07:52.069
Sorry, if I'm in a busy kitchen,

07:52.196 --> 07:54.949
I'm gonna have to scream
at someone gordon ramsay style.

07:55.036 --> 07:58.416
A raw egg?
You're gonna kill someone!

07:58.502 --> 07:59.961
20 years of being
in the business,

08:00.089 --> 08:02.842
And you're the biggest buffoon
I've ever met.

08:02.929 --> 08:04.931
Now let's step outside,
where I'll speak to you

08:05.016 --> 08:06.726
In an entirely different tone.

08:06.854 --> 08:09.191
What's going on with you?
Tell me.

08:09.235 --> 08:10.610
I don't, I don't know.

08:10.738 --> 08:12.448
You're overwhelmed
trying to live up

08:12.617 --> 08:14.369
To your father's expectations,
aren't you?

08:14.454 --> 08:15.914
Yeah, I guess.

08:15.999 --> 08:18.921
Listen, your father nikos
was a proud greek man

08:19.006 --> 08:20.716
Who came to this country
with nothing but

08:20.802 --> 08:22.053
A baklava and a dream.

08:22.180 --> 08:24.142
But he's gone now,
and you have to accept that.

08:24.227 --> 08:27.148
Now, those people in there
need a leader, not a friend.

08:27.317 --> 08:28.151
Understood?

08:28.319 --> 08:30.489
Yes. Thank you, chef ramsay.

08:30.616 --> 08:31.993
I have tremendous respect
for you

08:32.078 --> 08:34.248
And what you do
for people's businesses.

08:34.333 --> 08:35.709
Good. Now, just don't yelp

08:35.794 --> 08:37.004
Any places from the show

08:37.089 --> 08:39.927
Or eat at any of my restaurants
in las vegas.

08:43.395 --> 08:44.437
[phone chimes]

08:44.565 --> 08:45.773
Oh, from peter.

08:45.901 --> 08:49.574
"turn on channel five
right now."

08:49.659 --> 08:52.789
<i>[peter]
 welcome to the first episode
 of bar table talk.</i>

08:52.917 --> 08:56.465
<i> Finally, a show for men
 by men. Football.</i>

08:56.592 --> 08:58.552
[groans]
you've got to be kidding me.

08:58.597 --> 09:00.349
Now check out
our theme song called

09:00.517 --> 09:02.019
"guys just want to have fun,"

09:02.146 --> 09:03.940
Which is just each of us
yelling "guys"

09:04.025 --> 09:05.568
Over the parts
where they sing "girls"

09:05.655 --> 09:07.030
In "girls just want
to have fun."

09:07.115 --> 09:10.455
<i>♪ when the working day is done ♪</i>

09:10.540 --> 09:11.917
<i>-♪ oh ♪
-guys.</i>

09:12.002 --> 09:14.255
<i>♪ they want to have fun ♪</i>

09:14.383 --> 09:15.591
<i>-♪ oh ♪
-guys.</i>

09:15.677 --> 09:18.055
<i>-♪ just want to have... ♪
-guys.</i>

09:18.140 --> 09:21.939
<i>♪ they want, want to have fun ♪</i>

09:22.024 --> 09:23.944
<i>-♪ girls... ♪
-guys!</i>

09:24.029 --> 09:25.029
<i>[peter]
 damn it, joe.</i>

09:25.115 --> 09:26.031
<i>[joe]
 this is why I wanted to use</i>

09:26.118 --> 09:27.451
<i> "the boys are back in town."</i>

09:27.537 --> 09:29.957
<i> But no!</i>

09:32.340 --> 09:34.050
Welcome back. Now it's time for

09:34.136 --> 09:36.848
The clenched-buttocks
urinal-fart of the day,

09:36.975 --> 09:40.356
Sent in by gene kozlowski
at imperial tool and dye

09:40.442 --> 09:41.860
In kenosha, wisconsin.

09:41.903 --> 09:43.154
Let her rip, gene.

09:43.239 --> 09:45.242
[farting]

09:47.206 --> 09:48.666
Ah.

09:48.794 --> 09:50.671
You just know
that one had the power

09:50.798 --> 09:52.592
Of a state fair sausage
behind it.

09:52.720 --> 09:53.928
Impressive stuff.

09:54.056 --> 09:57.019
Coming up, all the people
from your wife's work

09:57.104 --> 10:00.401
She claims are horrible
who, surprise, aren't.

10:00.487 --> 10:01.821
Ugh, disgusting.

10:01.948 --> 10:03.575
I can't believe
that's my husband.

10:03.702 --> 10:05.120
Although I shouldn't be
surprised

10:05.206 --> 10:06.917
After what happened
on our wedding night.

10:07.002 --> 10:11.009
[chuckles]
peter, are you ready?

10:11.136 --> 10:13.013
Sorry, I already masturbated.

10:13.099 --> 10:14.726
There was a seashell
on top of the toilet

10:14.812 --> 10:16.480
That looked like a boob.

10:20.408 --> 10:21.533
Okay, lunch is over.

10:21.618 --> 10:23.036
We got more cookie orders
to take care of.

10:23.122 --> 10:26.753
All right, let's get
our sister crying.

10:26.839 --> 10:29.760
<i>♪ I was all right ♪</i>

10:29.846 --> 10:32.516
<i>♪ for a while ♪</i>

10:32.601 --> 10:37.026
<i>♪ I could smile for a while ♪</i>

10:37.195 --> 10:39.157
<i>♪ but I saw you last night ♪</i>

10:39.242 --> 10:42.789
<i>♪ you held my hand so tight ♪</i>

10:42.916 --> 10:47.049
<i>♪ as you stopped to say hello ♪</i>

10:47.177 --> 10:49.763
<i>♪ oh, you wished me well ♪</i>

10:49.891 --> 10:53.314
<i>♪ you couldn't tell ♪</i>

10:53.432 --> 10:57.239
<i>♪ that I'd been crying ♪</i>

10:57.366 --> 10:59.703
<i>♪ over you ♪</i>

10:59.830 --> 11:04.714
<i>♪ crying over you ♪</i>

11:04.841 --> 11:09.475
<i>♪ when you said "so long." ♪</i>

11:11.315 --> 11:12.900
<i>[peter]
 and that's why the eagles are</i>

11:12.985 --> 11:15.531
<i> The best yard work band
 of all time.</i>

11:15.658 --> 11:17.159
<i>[joe]
 I'm sorry, are we in a world</i>

11:17.245 --> 11:19.874
<i> Where the steve miller band
 was never born?</i>

11:19.960 --> 11:22.120
Oh, this show gets dumber
by the second.

11:22.215 --> 11:23.715
-[doorbell rings]
-just come in!

11:23.802 --> 11:26.764
Who even cares anymore?
Oh, hi, daddy.

11:26.849 --> 11:28.101
What are you doing here?

11:28.228 --> 11:31.275
Oh, I stopped by to...
Oh, no way. I love this show.

11:31.402 --> 11:32.360
Oh, is meg around?

11:32.446 --> 11:34.198
-She's in the kitchen.
-Excellent.

11:34.325 --> 11:36.160
Well, aren't you gonna ask
how I'm doing?

11:36.246 --> 11:39.502
Lois, I can see
one, two, three ant traps.

11:39.588 --> 11:42.926
I know how you're doing.
Oh, four.

11:45.768 --> 11:46.935
Oh, hey, carter.

11:47.021 --> 11:48.230
What are you doing here,
grandpa?

11:48.399 --> 11:50.109
Word has gotten around
about your cookies,

11:50.236 --> 11:52.239
And I have a business
opportunity for you.

11:52.325 --> 11:54.369
I'm throwing a party
for my billionaire friends

11:54.455 --> 11:56.457
On Friday, and I'd like you
to cater it.

11:56.542 --> 11:58.712
Oh, my god! We'd love to.

11:58.756 --> 12:00.507
Uh, meg, maybe let a graduate

12:00.593 --> 12:03.473
Of the howard schultz
masterclass handle this.

12:03.516 --> 12:05.436
I'm prepared to offer you
10,000--

12:05.521 --> 12:06.813
-We'll do it.
-Pennies.

12:06.899 --> 12:09.362
10,000 pennies, or $100.

12:09.489 --> 12:11.074
Oh, dude, you blew it.

12:11.159 --> 12:13.871
Just kidding, I'm super rich.
I'll pay you 50 grand.

12:13.999 --> 12:17.254
Holy crap, $50,000!

12:17.382 --> 12:20.929
I'll need 500 bags of cookies.
All right, see you Friday.

12:21.014 --> 12:23.519
Ugh, I really don't want to have
to talk to your mother again.

12:23.646 --> 12:26.358
Guess I'll just airpods it out.

12:26.443 --> 12:28.113
[lois]
bye, daddy.

12:28.240 --> 12:30.075
<i>I said bye, daddy.</i>

12:30.160 --> 12:32.080
[door opens, shuts]

12:34.921 --> 12:36.673
You guys, I just want
to thank you

12:36.759 --> 12:38.886
For helping make my cookies
such a success.

12:39.013 --> 12:40.850
It really means a lot to me.

12:40.935 --> 12:42.437
And for the first time
in my life,

12:42.480 --> 12:44.734
I'm finally feeling
proud of myself

12:44.819 --> 12:46.446
And hopeful about my future.

12:46.573 --> 12:49.953
I think... I think
I'm actually happy.

12:50.081 --> 12:52.083
Oh, that's great to hear, meg.

12:52.169 --> 12:53.503
We're proud of you, too.

12:53.589 --> 12:57.304
Now we got cookies to make.
Give us those tears.

12:57.431 --> 13:00.101
[straining]

13:03.319 --> 13:06.240
Oh, I know.
Meg, when you were a baby,

13:06.367 --> 13:08.077
You were left at a fire station.

13:08.164 --> 13:12.254
And those firemen left you
at another fire station.

13:13.760 --> 13:15.386
The only reason you had a date
for homecoming

13:15.472 --> 13:18.727
Was because the guy got
community service hours for it.

13:20.608 --> 13:22.820
Oh, no. I can't cry.

13:22.947 --> 13:24.950
A-and when I hear about
my crappy old life,

13:25.077 --> 13:27.832
I just feel proud and happy
about where I am now.

13:27.917 --> 13:30.420
Uh-oh, no tears means
no cookies.

13:30.464 --> 13:33.093
Which also means
no cookie business.

13:33.178 --> 13:36.560
Hi, I'm jamie lee curtis,
and I heard someone here

13:36.645 --> 13:38.940
Was having a problem
with feminine dryness.

13:39.025 --> 13:40.986
Oh, I-I think I'm all set.

13:41.071 --> 13:43.241
Have you tried
sliquid feminine wash,

13:43.326 --> 13:45.956
The natural solution
to feminine dryness?

13:46.083 --> 13:47.501
Oh, no, no.

13:47.587 --> 13:50.173
I-I-I think we have
different problems, dawg.

13:50.259 --> 13:51.510
Well, I'd hear her out.

13:51.596 --> 13:54.434
Sliquid's the one feminine wash
that goes on dry

13:54.519 --> 13:55.895
And doesn't drip.

13:55.980 --> 13:58.025
Chris, are you selling
intimacy products

13:58.152 --> 13:59.278
With jamie lee curtis?

13:59.405 --> 14:02.619
Well, stewie, I'd say
sliquid sells itself.

14:02.704 --> 14:04.665
[chris and jamie laugh]

14:04.751 --> 14:06.502
It goes on dry?

14:12.936 --> 14:14.270
Meg, I don't want to alarm you,

14:14.356 --> 14:16.943
But if you can't cry,
we won't get the $50,000

14:17.028 --> 14:18.404
From carter for catering
his party.

14:18.490 --> 14:19.950
I know, I'm sorry.

14:20.035 --> 14:22.580
It's just that, since the cookie
business became successful,

14:22.667 --> 14:23.875
I'm not sad anymore.

14:23.961 --> 14:26.005
Well, there goes my dream
of becoming

14:26.091 --> 14:27.801
The next otis spunkmeyer.

14:27.886 --> 14:30.223
Your dream is to be
otis spunkmeyer?

14:30.308 --> 14:34.023
I love a company that works
a dirty word for a bodily fluid

14:34.067 --> 14:35.109
Into their name.

14:35.194 --> 14:37.406
Chris, that is absolutely
disgusting.

14:37.575 --> 14:40.371
Hey, the way I see it,
in this life,

14:40.540 --> 14:42.710
Ya gotta laugh.

14:45.050 --> 14:47.762
God, he said "ya gotta laugh"
so many times,

14:47.890 --> 14:49.475
It started to feel
like a threat.

14:49.602 --> 14:51.187
Why did we come to this again?

14:51.273 --> 14:53.401
Remember that kid I hit
with my mail truck?

14:53.486 --> 14:56.282
-That was the kid?
-That was the kid.

14:58.874 --> 15:02.046
Ladies, I'm at the end
of my rope with this damn show.

15:02.131 --> 15:04.216
Peter's become impossible
to live with.

15:04.344 --> 15:06.555
Yeah, cleveland thinks
he's fancy, too.

15:06.683 --> 15:08.935
<i>You know, he's demanding
pert plus now</i>

15:09.022 --> 15:10.522
Instead of regular old pert.

15:10.650 --> 15:12.486
Joe's also gotten
a big head lately.

15:12.571 --> 15:15.326
When he eats graham crackers
now, he totally ignores

15:15.495 --> 15:17.538
The suggested perforations.

15:17.666 --> 15:19.293
He's like a mad king.

15:19.420 --> 15:21.047
We've got to shut
this show down.

15:21.132 --> 15:22.801
Oh, I don't know.

15:22.844 --> 15:24.972
Lois, have you heard
what peter said

15:25.100 --> 15:26.351
On yesterday's show?

15:26.478 --> 15:28.396
<i>[peter]
 and so I say, men,</i>

15:28.524 --> 15:30.318
<i> We deserve a second drawer.</i>

15:30.403 --> 15:33.282
<i> It should be four to two,
 not five to one.</i>

15:33.369 --> 15:34.702
[gasps]

15:34.788 --> 15:39.798
Ladies, it's time to put an end
to their little show.

15:44.561 --> 15:46.479
Now, remember, when they
start talking about

15:46.565 --> 15:49.153
How awful women are,
we storm the stage,

15:49.238 --> 15:50.573
Call them out on it.

15:50.741 --> 15:54.865
And then we'll go viral
and the show will be canceled.

15:54.959 --> 15:56.460
<i>Welcome to bar table talk.</i>

15:56.588 --> 15:58.131
Fellas, what's on your mind
today?

15:58.216 --> 15:59.968
Is it me, or does it seem
like no one knows how

16:00.054 --> 16:02.600
To coil a garden hose anymore?

16:04.522 --> 16:06.358
Remember sports guys you liked?

16:06.485 --> 16:09.657
-Oh, yeah.
-Totally.
-I like those guys.

16:12.290 --> 16:14.585
Um, you know what,
let's take a break.

16:14.670 --> 16:15.838
We'll be right back.

16:15.965 --> 16:19.137
-Oh, my god, it's happening.
-What's happening?

16:19.223 --> 16:20.933
Ah, what are we doing?

16:21.018 --> 16:24.232
I started this 'cause there were
no daytime talk shows with men,

16:24.318 --> 16:26.947
And lois said that's because men
eventually run out of things

16:27.074 --> 16:28.325
To say to each other.

16:28.410 --> 16:31.374
Well, looks like she was right.

16:33.171 --> 16:35.131
I don't want to be right.

16:35.217 --> 16:37.595
Lois? What are you all
doing here?

16:37.682 --> 16:40.185
We came down
to get this show canceled.

16:40.271 --> 16:41.730
Between the embarrassing content

16:41.816 --> 16:44.069
And you becoming so full
of yourself at home,

16:44.113 --> 16:45.739
Well, I thought it was
the only option.

16:45.825 --> 16:47.995
But when I heard you admit
you were wrong,

16:48.080 --> 16:51.377
I remembered why I married you
in the first place.

16:51.504 --> 16:54.217
Because I proposed in an
offensive chinese accent,

16:54.303 --> 16:55.762
And you just wanted to
get out of the restaurant?

16:55.889 --> 16:58.936
No, peter, because beneath
all your craziness,

16:59.022 --> 17:02.277
I know there's just a sweet,
confused child.

17:02.404 --> 17:04.365
-Can I get a lizard?
-No, peter.

17:04.451 --> 17:05.492
But you said!

17:05.578 --> 17:07.288
Fine, you can get a lizard.

17:07.373 --> 17:09.209
I love you, mom lois.

17:09.295 --> 17:11.005
I love you, too, peter.

17:11.132 --> 17:13.803
Can you watch my lizard?
I'm bored of it.

17:17.271 --> 17:18.689
You really think
seeing a therapist

17:18.775 --> 17:20.401
Is the best way
to get me to cry?

17:20.487 --> 17:23.241
Absolutely. And this guy is
the best in town.

17:23.327 --> 17:25.538
See you next week, john.

17:25.624 --> 17:26.791
Looking forward to it.

17:26.918 --> 17:29.046
Man, there's nothing to do
for that guy,

17:29.173 --> 17:30.883
But he's got insurance.

17:30.927 --> 17:33.013
Okay, who's meg griffin?

17:35.814 --> 17:38.818
So, I'm dr. Matthews,
but you can call me brad.

17:38.904 --> 17:41.482
My delta chi brothers
used to call me crusher,

17:41.535 --> 17:43.161
So that's fair game, too.

17:43.288 --> 17:44.540
Wow, this guy rocks.

17:44.667 --> 17:46.837
Before we start,
it's important to know

17:46.922 --> 17:48.340
I only accept crypto.

17:48.384 --> 17:51.179
So bitcoin, dogecoin
or ethereum.

17:51.265 --> 17:53.435
Oh, actually, wait.
Not ethereum.

17:53.562 --> 17:55.773
Wait, wait, no.
I-I don't, I don't anymore.

17:55.900 --> 17:58.404
Wait, yes, yes, I do,
but you have to send it,

17:58.532 --> 17:59.574
-Like, right now.
-[phone beeps]

17:59.701 --> 18:01.119
-Did you send it?
-I did.

18:01.204 --> 18:03.165
No! Why did you do that?!

18:03.293 --> 18:06.255
Ooh, "forget real estate.
Invest in money

18:06.383 --> 18:08.343
You can't even see," they said.

18:08.512 --> 18:11.810
Okay, I guess let's talk
about you.

18:11.896 --> 18:15.193
Well, earlier this week, I cried
into some cookie dough,

18:15.320 --> 18:18.533
And my tears actually made
the cookies taste incredible.

18:18.619 --> 18:21.832
So we started a successful
cookie business using my tears.

18:21.918 --> 18:24.464
But now I'm too happy
to cry anymore.

18:24.508 --> 18:27.011
But no tears means no money.

18:27.138 --> 18:29.433
Meg, have you considered
the reason you're happy

18:29.519 --> 18:31.103
Isn't because of the business?

18:31.189 --> 18:34.027
That maybe it's because
you finally got to spend

18:34.112 --> 18:37.034
Quality time bonding with
the family members you love?

18:37.119 --> 18:40.625
Oh, snap. My man crusher
dropping knowledge bombs.

18:40.752 --> 18:44.175
Guys, is the money really worth
the sister you love

18:44.261 --> 18:46.430
Feeling badly about herself?

18:49.481 --> 18:51.275
-No.
-It's not.

18:51.360 --> 18:53.237
The new thom browne line
is out next week,

18:53.407 --> 18:54.949
So maybe?

18:55.077 --> 18:58.124
Wow, I can't believe
you'd choose my happiness

18:58.293 --> 18:59.961
Over all that money, you guys.

19:00.088 --> 19:01.631
That really means a lot.

19:01.758 --> 19:03.636
We just want you
to be happy, meg.

19:03.722 --> 19:06.142
Chris is right. We love you.

19:06.269 --> 19:08.981
Oh, I love you guys.

19:12.867 --> 19:14.661
Hey, where's that diploma from?

19:14.830 --> 19:16.415
Oh, that's not a diploma.

19:16.542 --> 19:18.712
That's a certificate for
finishing the big bertha

19:18.797 --> 19:21.092
At leo's bar and grill
in cincinnati.

19:21.178 --> 19:24.350
Got a t-shirt, too,
but it's at the dry cleaners.

19:24.435 --> 19:26.270
Wow. Dry cleaning a t-shirt

19:26.398 --> 19:28.902
Bragging about a regional
food challenge?

19:28.987 --> 19:31.074
That's the dream.

19:33.956 --> 19:37.380
Honey, it's me. They fell
for the whole crusher routine.

19:37.465 --> 19:39.425
Oh, and their little
cookie business?

19:39.511 --> 19:43.601
Let's just say I...
Took care of it.

19:48.648 --> 19:50.743
[sinister laughter]

19:52.332 --> 19:54.584
[sinister laughter]

19:55.338 --> 19:57.550
[sinister laughter]

19:59.055 --> 20:00.975
[sinister laughter]

20:02.438 --> 20:05.610
[siren wailing]

20:05.738 --> 20:07.322
What happened last night?

20:07.450 --> 20:09.619
Oh, nothing. Just...
Just hit a home run

20:09.747 --> 20:11.206
In my softball game.

20:11.333 --> 20:13.243
No, I mean,
I mean the building.

20:13.337 --> 20:15.632
Huh? Oh, huge gas leak.

20:15.718 --> 20:17.554
Won the game.
Everybody's dead.

20:23.152 --> 20:26.365
Sorry I got carried away with
my daytime talk show, lois.

20:26.493 --> 20:28.286
Oh, peter, I'm just glad
you're home

20:28.372 --> 20:30.876
And still wearing television
makeup for some reason.

20:31.003 --> 20:33.215
I don't know what you're
talking about.

20:33.300 --> 20:35.845
Hey, sorry your cookie business
didn't work out, meg.

20:35.931 --> 20:37.767
Yeah, I guess it would have
been pretty sweet

20:37.894 --> 20:40.606
To have a successful
cookie business, but it's fine.

20:40.733 --> 20:43.070
You know, meg, the way I see it,

20:43.155 --> 20:45.910
Life's too darn short.

20:48.459 --> 20:49.919
Boy, that was brutal.

20:49.963 --> 20:51.798
Yeah, what a big waste of time.

20:51.883 --> 20:54.847
I know, it's like life really is
too darn short.

20:54.890 --> 20:57.687
Huh. Maybe it was good.

20:57.772 --> 21:00.025
Screw it, I'm getting a shirt.